# Evidence and reasoning invariants

Preserve:

- Change Intent ≠ Deployment ≠ realized Change;
- anticipated effect ≠ normative Expectation;
- Deployment attempt ≠ intent association ≠ activation ≠ intended effect realized;
- Expectation ≠ Baseline;
- planned value ≠ empirical Baseline;
- prospective reference preparation ≠ realized reference transition;
- Observation ≠ Assessment;
- missing evidence ≠ observed absence;
- typical ≠ healthy;
- atypical ≠ degraded/defective;
- successful execution ≠ freshness ≠ data quality;
- planned topology ≠ active Lineage;
- Lineage reachability ≠ cause ≠ confirmed Impact;
- Change ≠ degradation ≠ cause;
- Investigation ≠ source evidence/causal truth;
- Causal Claim ≠ confirmed cause;
- Impact candidate ≠ exposure ≠ downstream effect ≠ business consequence;
- Annotation ≠ Observation/Change Intent/Expectation/causal confirmation;
- Explanation ≠ independent truth source;
- effective/event time ≠ recorded/knowledge time;
- correlation ≠ attribution ≠ confirmed cause.

Rules:

- Time/history is first-class and uses ledger-like append/supersede/correction semantics for material state.
- Material conclusions remain traceable to provenance-bearing evidence.
- Change Intent may independently trigger prospective Expectation review and a prospective Baseline comparability break.
- Planned anticipated behavior becomes normative only through explicit Expectation establishment/revision.
- Intended values never become Baseline evidence.
- Intent-to-Deployment association requires provenance-bearing linkage evidence; temporal proximity alone is insufficient.
- Workflow success/planned time cannot by themselves activate reference transition.
- Reference transition requires sufficient realization evidence for the relevant subject/dimension/context.
- Baseline non-comparability is context/time scoped; structural transitions do not delete historical Baselines.
- Rollback/restoration requires comparability/applicability re-resolution and cannot blindly revive earlier references.
- Partial/canary/environment transitions stay scoped to the affected context.
- Post-transition Baseline requires sufficient comparable post-transition Observations.
- An applicable Expectation can support immediate post-change Assessment before the new Baseline exists.
- Missing telemetry never becomes zero/no-event.
- Assessments retain exact Observation and Expectation/Baseline versions/basis.
- Health dimensions stay separate unless an explicit aggregation rule exists.
- Lineage is typed, temporal, historical, authorization-aware, and graph-compatible.
- Investigation may organize evidence but cannot promote a causal claim merely to close the inquiry.
- Preserve supporting and contradicting evidence on every material Causal Claim.
- Never infer cause from Deployment timing, Lineage, realized Change, intent consistency, or absence of competing evidence alone.
- Multiple contributing causes and unresolved outcomes are valid.
- `confirmed` requires an explicit accepted evidence/authority standard.
- Downstream traversal yields Impact candidates only; independently evaluate exposure, downstream state/effect, and business consequence.
- Human Annotation remains human-authored context; structured truths belong to their owning concepts.
- Explanation is an authorized, time-aware projection over concept state with material statement-to-basis traceability.
- Distinguish contemporaneous knowledge from retrospective knowledge when later evidence changes intent/activation/reference interpretation.
- Do not select graph database, event store, blockchain, persistence architecture, LLM, or causal algorithm merely because the semantics are graph/ledger/explanation-friendly.
